WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>Menchi-Katsu</b>

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.370
So that's three whatsontaps.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.080
Thank you very much

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.260
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.260
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.080
Things have been so peaceful lately.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.680
Yeah.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.130
When it's this quiet,
I'm going to get all soft!

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.440
Any kind of incident would be nice.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.130
Can't we have some action?

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.870
Don't say things like that.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.370
Welcome!

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.100
Welcome.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:05.930
Welcome.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.380
<b>Corona (58) 
Original proprietor of 
the "Flying Wheel Inn"</b>

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.380
<b>Rolf (63) 
Original proprietor of 
the "Flying Wheel Inn"</b>

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.450
Are you open for business?

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:08.160
Yes!

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.370
For two, right?

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.470
Please sit wherever you like.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:15.310
Won't you consider marrying into our family?

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.190
Excuse me?

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.260
What did you just say?

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.330
We want you to come to 
marry into our family.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.560
What?!

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.850
You'd be just perfect for our grandson!

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.570
Please, take over the 
duty of running our inn!

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:33.240
But I can't just do that all of that sudden.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.100
You're right.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.470
Then we'll wait.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.070
How about an arranged marriage meeting?

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.980
A-Arranged marriage?

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.990
But why me?

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:47.240
I've seen how hard you work
here the past few days.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:50.240
With my face covered, I've 
been coming to watch you.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.520
I've been watching you morning and night

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.270
for a long, long, long, long, long time.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:56.800
She's creepy!

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.740
Yes, but this could turn 
into something good.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.340
I'm sure that you're the one.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.510
You would be an excellent proprietress.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.440
But I'm not interested in marriage yet.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.470
Don't say that.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:12.190
But...

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.170
I'm sorry she's so getting so intense.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:19.240
Once our Corona gets an idea in her 
head, she stops seeing anything else.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.330
It's fine.

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:21.800
It's nice to meet you.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:26.020
I'm Rolf from the Flying Wheel Inn.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.240
Hello.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.960
Flying Wheel Inn?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.460
You mean that meat restaurant?

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:34.040
You have heard of our renowned dish?

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.750
It's my favorite!

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.950
Thank you so much.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.050
What kind of dish is it?

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.280
You're saying you've never 
heard of our famous dish?

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:47.400
Please excuse my ignorance.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.050
It's a dish called Fleischpflanzerl.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.780
It's fried patty of ground meat.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.170
So something like hamburg steak.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.430
So you're tagging along 
with the missus today?

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:06.290
Well, there's that, but I also wanted 
to try this famous restaurant.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.170
I see.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.000
It seems they are both 
on fire or something...

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.880
Someone in the same industry 
as him came to try the food.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.090
Taishou has no choice but to get fired up.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.570
You can make whichever dish you like.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:22.690
As you wish.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.090
Shinobu-chan, I need your help.

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:26.020
Yes.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.350
I'm sorry, I have to go work now.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.450
Will you come back and have a long chat 
with me once your work is through?

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.120
S-Sure.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.040
Are you okay?

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:43.190
I really don't know about that 
arranged marriage thing.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:45.980
I'm fine though.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.980
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:52.270
So, are Taishou-san and 
Shinobu-san seeing each other?

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.340
I don't think so.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.660
And is there anyone else?

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:57.610
I don't know...

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.040
Taishou, what's that?

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:03.400
It's venison.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.950
I've been marinating the meat 
Frank-san gave me in yogurt.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.720
Why yogurt?

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:13.550
Because it takes away the gamy smell 
of the meat and tenderizes it.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.290
Huh.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:17.200
I wonder if that really works.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:20.540
You've been experimenting a lot lately.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:21.770
You think so?

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:26.130
You didn't used to work with 
ingredients you didn't know.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.470
I guess we had that Schnitzel incident.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.890
I've been thinking that
I want to start incorporating

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:34.350
more of this land's techniques 
and ingredients.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.330
First, you cut the meat into thin slices.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.810
Then you chop it into ground meat.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.320
You finely dice the onion.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.830
Add the meat and spices, and mix it well.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.560
Once the mixture is firm enough, 
you form it into patties.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:54.070
You roll the patties in flour, egg, and panko

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:55.800
and then...

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.580
<b>Sizzle sizzle sizzle</b>

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:57.570
You fry them!

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:59.770
That's a lot of steps.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.710
I'm looking forward to the finished result.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.230
Look at that form.

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.550
It's perfect.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.260
It really is.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:13.560
<b>Venison Menchi-Katsu</b>

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:13.560
<b>Even tougher venison can become 
easy to eat with a few tricks!</b>

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.480
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.610
This is venison menchi-katsu.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:20.200
Don't worry. I made some for you, too.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.060
Good work, Taishou!

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.400
We can always count on you!

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:32.570
Here we go.

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.480
<b>Crunch crunch</b>

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:37.310
Hot...

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.280
So good. The breading is so crispy.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.590
I can't smell the gaminess 
of the meat one bit.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.010
I see.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:52.470
This is delicious.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:58.420
The wild meat of a deer raised in the forest,

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:02.050
artfully sealed into the breading.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.900
I'm glad you're back to your normal self.

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:09.820
It's because I heard the 
guests enjoying their food.

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:12.320
That is tasty, beyond a doubt.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:17.810
But I can't say it's better than 
the Fleischpflanzerl we serve.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.130
What do you think?

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:20.830
You're right.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:24.530
You can try these too if you like.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:29.240
Is this mustard and a sauce?

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.260
Yeah, it's Worcestershire sauce.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.650
It really goes well with it.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:34.480
Is that so?

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.780
I'll try it.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:47.340
<b>Crunch crunch crunch</b>

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.660
It's rather light, but the taste is so rich.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:59.660
<b>Fizz</b>

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:01.460
Amazing!

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.890
It really makes the whatsontap even better!

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:03.960
Taishou!

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.570
I'll have another whatsontap!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:06.920
Me, too.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:13.410
<i>The sauce and mustard's tang and spice 
has catapulted the taste to new heights!</i>

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.980
<i>This is no longer any ordinary deer.</i>

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:20.380
<i>This is the golden stag, 
the stuff of legends.</i>

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:23.820
It was plenty good without 
the sauce too, but the sauce

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:27.160
pairs wonderfully with the 
fresh taste of cabbage.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:31.150
Taishou-san, I underestimated you.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.910
You've inspired me to try harder 
at my own restaurant as well.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:37.640
Hearing that is the highest praise.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:41.600
Looks like the venison 
menchi-katsu was a hit!

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.930
I think it was good that I kept 
it in that yogurt for so long.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:48.510
We should try some other kind of meat next.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.110
Right.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.650
Takes you back, doesn't it?

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:51.510
That's right.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:54.890
<b>Flying Wheel Inn</b>

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:54.900
It's been 40 years since 
we opened our restaurant.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.230
We've been through a lot together.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:08:03.070
But we were able to carry on 
because we had each other.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.810
I'm sure this restaurant will be the same.

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:08.090
That's right.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:11.590
Just like this cabbage and menchi katsu,

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.360
you need them both, or it doesn't work.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:16.970
Darling.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.190
Yes, I know.

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.240
Hello!

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.800
Welcome.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:23.480
<b>Frank (22)
 Butcher and regular
customer at Nobu</b>

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:23.490
Hey.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.370
Hey. You're coming in late.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:28.960
Yeah, work ran late.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.440
And besides...

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:35.260
Who's that kid?

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.640
I found him wandering around 
the alley around here.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.000
When I asked him, he said he 
had business in this restaurant.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.480
Wolfram!

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.920
Grandma!

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.730
I'm sorry. He's my grandson!

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.830
Did you come all the way here by yourself?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:51.650
Yeah.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.360
You were taking so long.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.630
And then I got lost on the way.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:00.340
As long as it ends well!

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:02.910
You came to find your grandma, huh?

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:05.850
Wait, so this is your grandson?

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.290
That's right.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:10.250
This is the one I wanted you 
to meet to discuss marriage.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:15.260
A-And just... how old are we?

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:17.640
<b>Wolfram (7)
 Rolf and Corona's grandson</b>

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:17.630
I'm seven!

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:21.810
Ma'am, pardon me for asking,

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:25.270
but just how old do you 
think Shinobu-chan is?

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:32.520
Well, I was thinking she was 14 or 15, 
but maybe I was mistaken.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:38.020
I'm 23.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:39.080
Oh, my.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.450
Then I apologize!

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:43.940
I completely misjudged your age.

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.700
It's not a problem.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.860
We are so terribly sorry.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:51.900
Looks like their ages are too 
far apart to discuss marriage.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.270
Please don't worry about it.

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.930
I appreciate the sentiment.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:01.290
Well, a lot has transpired, 
but thank you, Corona-san,

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.680
Rolf-san, and Wolfram-kun for bringing some

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:08.040
interesting times here to our peaceful Nobu.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.060
The regulars here are going to 
be talking about Shinobu-chan's

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:14.550
arranged marriage tale for quite some time!

00:10:15.190 --> 00:10:18.570
Then, a toast to Shinobu-chan's 
bright, single future!

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.530
Prosit!

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:27.370
This feels weird.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up is Nobu Plus!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:40.030
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:39.510
You can make real menchi-katsu 
even without frying it in oil?!

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:45.860
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:47.040
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:49.060
Corona-san was one intense grandma, huh?

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:49.720
Certainly!

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:51.170
Marrying her grandson...

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:51.620
Yeah...

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:54.570
Maybe people from the parallel
universe think Japanese people

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:59.720
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:59.720
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.910
look younger than they are. I mean
Shinobu-chan was thought to be 14 or 15.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:59.720
<b>Senke Shinobu</b>

00:10:57.910 --> 00:10:59.640
That only happens when you're still young.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:03.610
The menchi-katsu Taishou made looked really 
good, so I wanted to make that as well.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.890
But making menchi-katsu at home 
is actually quite a lot of work.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:06.890
I know!

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:11.430
So today, I'm going to skip the frying 
step and make it "menchi-katsu style."

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:11.430
<b>Easy menchi-katsu without frying</b>

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:14.530
What? "Menchi-katsu style" meatloaf?

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:16.450
<b>Menchi-Katsu Style Meatloaf 
[Ingredients (serves 2)] 
 [Meat]
 Mixed ground meat   200 grams 
 Panko breadcrumbs   3 tablespoons 
 Egg   1 
 Salt    a little 
 Pepper   a little 
 [Breading] 
 Panko breadcrumbs   1/2 heaping cup 
 Oil   1 tablespoon 
 Water   1 tablespoon 
 Cabbage   1/8
 Lemon   To taste</b>

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:16.460
You mean you'll make it in the oven?

00:11:16.450 --> 00:13:06.760
<b>Menchi-katsu
 style meatloaf</b>

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.510
First, we're going to 
soften the ground meat.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.660
When you do this, please 
start with just the meat.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:23.270
That way, it'll get sticky and 
mix well with the thickener.

00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:25.920
My recommendation is to pound it 
with your knuckles like this.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:26.510
Huh? Why?!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:30.940
<b>First, pound the ground meat with 
your knuckles to make it sticky</b>

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:30.310
This way, the heat from your hands won't 
transfer to it and allow it to get sticky.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:31.080
I see.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.560
Next, I'd like to put in the 
ingredients of the thickener.

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:38.550
<b>Adding the thickener
 Add Panko (3 tablespoons), Egg (1), 
Salt (a little), Pepper (a little)</b>

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:38.560
Panko, egg, salt and pepper... 
this is a popular combo.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:41.870
Premixing the egg and panko a bit is good.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:46.740
Then, mix it into the meat. Massage 
it in like this so it's all in.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:47.550
Right.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:49.580
Once it's all in there, use 
your finger tips to mix it up.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.050
When the mix looks like this, it's ready.

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:54.160
The meat is ready!

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:55.820
Now the breading!

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.950
I'm adding the water first.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:01.150
The water prevents it from getting burned.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:06.990
Then, the oil. The oil makes the 
finish crunchy, as if it's fried.

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:09.570
<b>Add water and oil to panko and
mix well to have the breading ready</b>

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:08.990
Really mix it well in here.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:09.570
Got it.

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:13.680
Next, we're going to spread 
the meat onto aluminum foil.

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:19.020
Add some oil first, then 
spread it with your hands.

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:20.230
Just like that?

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:22.850
Get some oil on your hands as well.

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.090
Ah! So it won't stick to your hands!

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:28.550
Just like when making hamburgers, 
get the air out like this.

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:29.360
Roger!

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:32.260
After you get the air out, 
put them onto the foil.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:38.000
<b>The meat patty should be about 1 centimeter thick</b>

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:37.140
Stretch them out so they're 
roughly 1 centimeter thick.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:38.480
Not making them too thick is the trick.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:41.670
Sprinkle the panko with the 
water and oil on them.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:43.510
<b>Put the panko-water-oil mixture on top of the meat patties</b>

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:49.390
We're going to cook these now, 
but since the oil can run off,

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:50.960
let's make a wall with the foil.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.470
And now we put them in the toaster oven.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:55.140
That's all we need to do to get 
menchi-katsu with crispy breading?

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:57.230
In about 10 minutes.

00:12:57.230 --> 00:12:59.670
While the meat is cooking, 
finely slice the cabbage.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.040
You're always so good with the knife!

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:06.370
All right, they're done.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:09.730
The menchi-katsu that doesn't 
have to be fried, all done.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:20.280
<b>Menchi-Katsu Style Meatloaf</b>

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:14.300
Fried food goes really well 
with beer and ale, doesn't it?

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:17.940
But for those of you for whom frying 
at home is just a tad too much,

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:22.140
please do try this baking in the toaster
oven so it looks like it's fried trick.

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:26.890
I can't believe that menchi-katsu with its 
high difficulty can be done so easily!

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:33.020
<b>Today's high-speed footage</b>

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:31.290
The breading is crunchy, the inside is 
juicy! It's just like the real deal!

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.690
Everybody, you have to try this!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:58.010
<b>Next Time...  
The Spy and the Salad</b>

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:54.140
Next time on "Isekai Izakaya"
aka "Izakaya Nobu in Aitheria."

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.490
Please sample the tasty tales.
